<section xml:lang="en-US" xml:id="magpie-chatbot-lab-1" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Magpie Chatbot Lab</title>

  <introduction>
 
    <p>
      This is the original College Board Magpie lab from 2014.
    </p>
    <p>
      For the original Magpie lab, here is the College Board <url
      href="http://secure-media.collegeboard.org/digitalServices/pdf/ap/ap-compscia-magpie-lab-student-guide.pdf"
      visual="http://secure-media.collegeboard.org/digitalServices/pdf/ap/ap-compscia-magpie-lab-student-guide.pdf">
      Magpie Chatbot Lab Student Guide</url>.
    </p>
    <p>
      The Magpie lab creates a simple <term>chatbot</term> and provides practice with <c>String</c> methods 
      and conditionals. A <term>chatbot</term> is a computer program that tries to hold a conversation with a user. 
      The exercises below will walk you through the activities in the original Magpie chatbot lab.
    </p>
</introduction>
  

